@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2147 = private unnamed_addr constant [2651 x i8] c"## What it does\0A\0AChecks for use of standalone type variables and parameter specifications in generic classes.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A\0ASpecial type parameter syntax was introduced in Python 3.12 by [PEP 695] for defining generic\0Aclasses. This syntax is easier to read and provides cleaner support for generics.\0A\0A## Known problems\0A\0AThe rule currently skips generic classes nested inside of other functions or classes. It also\0Askips type parameters with the `default` argument introduced in [PEP 696] and implemented in\0APython 3.13.\0A\0AThis rule can only offer a fix if all of the generic types in the class definition are defined\0Ain the current module. For external type parameters, a diagnostic is emitted without a suggested\0Afix.\0A\0ANot all type checkers fully support PEP 695 yet, so even valid fixes suggested by this rule may\0Acause type checking to fail.\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis fix is marked as unsafe, as [PEP 695] uses inferred variance for type parameters, instead\0Aof the `covariant` and `contravariant` keywords used by `TypeVar` variables. As such, replacing\0Aa `TypeVar` variable with an inline type parameter may change its variance.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom typing import TypeVar\0A\0AT = TypeVar(\22T\22)\0A\0A\0Aclass GenericClass(Generic[T]):\0A    var: T\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aclass GenericClass[T]:\0A    var: T\0A```\0A\0A## See also\0A\0AThis rule replaces standalone type variables in classes but doesn't remove\0Athe corresponding type variables even if they are unused after the fix. See\0A[`unused-private-type-var`][PYI018] for a rule to clean up unused\0Aprivate type variables.\0A\0AThis rule will not rename private type variables to remove leading underscores, even though the\0Anew type parameters are restricted in scope to their associated class. See\0A[`private-type-parameter`][UP049] for a rule to update these names.\0A\0AThis rule will correctly handle classes with multiple base classes, as long as the single\0A`Generic` base class is at the end of the argument list, as checked by\0A[`generic-not-last-base-class`][PYI059]. If a `Generic` base class is\0Afound outside of the last position, a diagnostic is emitted without a suggested fix.\0A\0AThis rule only applies to generic classes and does not include generic functions. See\0A[`non-pep695-generic-function`][UP047] for the function version.\0A\0A[PEP 695]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0695/\0A[PEP 696]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0696/\0A[PYI018]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-private-type-var/\0A[PYI059]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/generic-not-last-base-class/\0A[UP047]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/non-pep695-generic-function/\0A[UP049]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/private-type-parameter/\0A", align 1
